      "why": "iterative already owns the entire merged front (13/13) with best luts_plus_ffs=257, so it is the only family that can plausibly improve the min-area objective. The previous search was broad; I now focus on the region where accuracy_bits is maximised for a given area: data_width 12-18 and n_iter 12-18 are the sweet spot where max_abs_err <= 2^-10 is met with minimal guard bits. Keeping angle_guard and frac_guard in their full ranges lets Optuna find the exact minimal-guard combinations that push accuracy_bits toward 10+ while keeping luts_plus_ffs near 257. The throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS) is easily met by iterative at reasonable Fmax since 1 result per N+3 cycles at ~100+ MHz gives >1 MSPS for N<=18."
    },
