  "rationale": "Round 1 found 8 feasible Pareto designs, all iterative or unrolled_k, with luts_plus_ffs 257-405 and accuracy 10.3-13.2 bits. The minimum-area design is iterative at 257 LUTs+FFs with 10.3 bits accuracy and 11 MSPS throughput. However, pipelined and pipelined_m families remain unexplored. These families produce 1 result/cycle, which may allow different area/throughput trade-offs. Since the spec prioritizes area (min luts_plus_ffs) with a loose throughput constraint (>=1 MSPS, easily met at 10+ MSPS), pipeline architectures could potentially reduce area by simplifying the datapath or improving Fmax. The accuracy constraint is comfortably met (best 13.2 bits vs required 10 bits), so there is room to trade accuracy for area if pipeline designs offer lower luts_plus_ffs. I will allocate 50% of the remaining 100 evals to pipelined and 50% to pipelined_m, focusing on the data_width 14-18 and n_iter 12-18 ranges where iterative found feasible designs, with angle_guard -1..2 and frac_guard 0..1 to keep area low while maintaining accuracy >=10 bits."
